:name: CANcestry T2 virtual bench - brownout (BOR) scenario
:description: Bring-up of the STM32G474-class platform model plus the BOR reset injector for the H-11 brownout scenario (issue #64).

# CANcestry T2 virtual bench - brownout bring-up script (H-11, issue #64).
#
# Implements: HW-SF-002 sub-events (ii) main-rail brownout to BOR level 3 and
# (iii) main-rail removal - the reset side of the retention claim - and
# HW-SF-004 (retention write before the rail reaches the BOR level), against
# the REAL v1.0.0 firmware (off-tree driver firmware/bor_brownout.c).
# Governing documents: docs/hw/virtual-bench-plan.md sections 1, 3, 6 and 8.5;
# docs/hw/tool-qualification.md section 3 (bor_reset_injector, TCL1) and
# section 4.6; HwAGENTS.md rules 1, 5, 6 and 13.
#
# WHY A THIRD .resc (issue #64 constraint 4, "extend, don't modify"): the
# H-07/H-08 retention bring-up (cancestry-hw.resc) and the H-10 CAN fault
# bring-up (cancestry-hw-fault.resc) are left byte-identical. This script loads
# the SAME unmodified platform description (stm32g474-cancestry.repl) and the
# SAME four scripted register models, and ADDS the BOR reset injector plus the
# brownout capture hooks.
#
# Driven by hw/virtual-bench/scenarios/t2_brownout_001.py (via
# hw/virtual-bench/t2_bor_common.py):
#
#   $elf   path of the brownout-scenario firmware ELF (mandatory; built
#          off-tree from tag v1.0.0 by hw/virtual-bench/firmware/
#          build_firmware.sh with CANCESTRY_T2_DRIVER=bor_brownout). Set by
#          the runner as a QUOTED path with NO '@' marker (bring-up finding
#          F-32); the guard below fails closed when it is missing.
#   $t2_seed  fixed deterministic seed, unquoted (bring-up finding F-31).
#          Must stay equal to fmi_bridge.FIXED_SEED.
#
# Determinism (HwAGENTS.md rule 5): the machine is left PAUSED and is advanced
# exclusively by the orchestrator's fixed-size `emulation RunFor` quanta
# (100 us master step, the H-07 bridge contract). No wall clock is consumed.

using sysbus

$t2_seed?=123456789

# Fail-closed guard: T2 executes a REAL v1.0.0 ELF (HW-PLAN section 8.3); the
# bench never falls back to a reimplementation of the firmware.
python "assert variables['elf'] not in ('', None), 'cancestry-hw-bor.resc: no firmware ELF provided (set $elf before including this script)'"
python "import Antmicro.Renode.Logging as _clog"
python "_clog.Logger.Info('[cancestry-hw-bor] step0: python logger channel OK, elf=%s' % variables['elf'])"

mach create "cancestry"
python "_clog.Logger.Info('[cancestry-hw-bor] step2: machine created')"

# Same platform description as the retention and fault bring-ups (unmodified).
# $ORIGIN-absolute path: bring-up finding F-24 (the process CWD of a headless
# Renode is the install directory, never this script's directory).
machine LoadPlatformDescription $ORIGIN/stm32g474-cancestry.repl
python "_clog.Logger.Info('[cancestry-hw-bor] step3: platform loaded')"

# The four scripted register models of the H-07 platform ($ORIGIN-absolute
# paths and QUOTED names: bring-up findings F-28 and F-30). All four stay
# registered: the brownout driver arms no IWDG, but the RCC model owns the
# reset-cause flags (RCC_CSR.BORRSTF is set by the injector through the bus,
# exactly as the IWDG model sets IWDGRSTF), and the RTC/BKP model owns the
# retention shadow the recovered fault code is read from.
machine PyDevFromFile $ORIGIN/iwdg_model.py 0x40003000 0x14 true "iwdg"
machine PyDevFromFile $ORIGIN/rtc_backup_model.py 0x40002800 0x64 false "rtc_backup"
machine PyDevFromFile $ORIGIN/gpioa_model.py 0x48000000 0x400 true "gpioa"
machine PyDevFromFile $ORIGIN/rcc_model.py 0x40021000 0x98 true "rcc"
python "_clog.Logger.Info('[cancestry-hw-bor] step3c: 4 register models registered')"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# H-11 EXTENSION: the BOR reset injector (issue #64 deliverable 4).
#
# Registered HERE rather than declared in stm32g474-cancestry.repl for the
# F-28 reason (a `filename:` attribute in a .repl is resolved CWD-relative
# inside the PythonPeripheral constructor, which breaks headless CI) and to
# keep the platform description file's behaviour byte-identical: the .repl
# receives the comment-only H-11 slot contract, zero behavioural change.
#
# Base 0x40001000 is the address the issue names. It is one guest page
# (bring-up finding F-29), an address the v1.0.0 firmware never touches
# (hal_stm32.c accesses only DWT/DEMCR, the FDCAN bases and - through
# watchdog.c - IWDG, RTC/BKP, GPIOA and RCC), and the platform declares no
# peripheral there, so the registration neither overlaps an existing model nor
# changes firmware-visible behaviour.
machine PyDevFromFile $ORIGIN/bor_reset_injector.py 0x40001000 0x400 true "bor_reset_injector"
python "_clog.Logger.Info('[cancestry-hw-bor] step3d: bor_reset_injector registered at 0x40001000')"

# Deterministic execution: fixed global quantum (the 100 us master step of the
# H-07 bridge contract) and the fixed seed for the only Renode randomness
# source. `emulation RunFor` advances virtual time exactly.
emulation SetGlobalQuantum "0.0001"
emulation SetSeed $t2_seed
python "_clog.Logger.Info('[cancestry-hw-bor] step4: quantum and seed set')"

sysbus LoadELF $elf
# Readback: the initial SP word of the vector table (0x20018000 per
# firmware/startup.s) proves the ELF segments reached flash.
python "bus = sysbus if 'sysbus' in dir() else (machine['sysbus'] if 'machine' in dir() else monitor.Machine['sysbus']); v = bus.ReadDoubleWord(0x08000000); _clog.Logger.Info('[cancestry-hw-bor] step5: vector SP=0x%08x (ELF loaded)' % v)"

# Trace-area magic: the H-07 contract word (the orchestrator refuses to run
# against a machine whose capture area was not initialized by a bring-up
# script).
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x60000000 0x54324353

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# H-11 slot initialization (the platform contract in
# stm32g474-cancestry.repl). The BOR injector keeps ALL of its state in the
# trace area (a Renode machine reset re-initializes scripted peripherals), so
# the preflight state is established HERE, once, before the machine runs:
#
#   NRST released (1), SRAM marker intact (0), injector status accepted (0),
#   all event stamps 0.
#
# The main-SRAM marker word (0x20017000) is the T2-declared SRAM location the
# firmware publishes its canary to and the injector discards on the BOR reset.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x60000008 0x00000000
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x60000070 0x00000000
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x60000074 0x00000000
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x60000078 0x00000000
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x6000007C 0x00000000
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x60000080 0x00000000
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x60000084 0x00000000
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x60000088 0x00000000
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x6000008C 0x00000000
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x60000104 0x00000001
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x60000108 0x00000000
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x6000010C 0x00000000
python "bus = monitor.Machine['sysbus']; _clog.Logger.Info('[cancestry-hw-bor] step7: t2_trace readback=0x%08x (expected 0x54324353) nrst_level=%d (expected 1 released)' % (bus.ReadDoubleWord(0x60000000), bus.ReadDoubleWord(0x60000104)))"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Brownout event capture (HwAGENTS.md rule 5: deterministic, hashed trace).
#
# The retention-write stamp reuses the H-08 slot 0x60000008, but
# FIRST-EVENT-ONLY: the driver publishes the retained terminal code once,
# before the brownout, and the ordering claim is about that first write. The
# guard makes the slot immune to any later retention-register write on the
# post-reset path (the platform's one-writer-per-slot contract).
#
# The two BOR stamps are symbol hooks on the off-tree driver's post-reset
# path (firmware/bor_brownout.c):
#
#   t2_bor_detect  entry of the post-BOR classification: the reset cause was
#                  read as BORRSTF and the retained fault code is recovered
#                  through the real v1.0.0 retention read API. Issue #64 asks
#                  for a hook "on the reset handler"; the v1.0.0 ELF ships no
#                  BOR classification in its reset handler (Reset_Handler in
#                  startup.s only initialises .data/.bss), so the hook is
#                  placed on the firmware's post-reset BOR detection entry
#                  (documented deviation, recorded in the scenario evidence
#                  and in tool-qualification.md section 4.6).
#   cancestry_hardware_set_safe_state  entry of the REAL v1.0.0 safe-state
#                  restoration function - the issue's "safe-state restoration
#                  function" - called on the post-reset path once the fault
#                  was detected.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
cpu AddSymbolHook "cancestry_watchdog_write_retention_register" """if machine['sysbus'].ReadDoubleWord(0x60000008) == 0:
machine['sysbus'].WriteDoubleWord(0x60000008, int(round(machine.ElapsedVirtualTime.TimeElapsed.TotalSeconds * 1000000)))
"""
cpu AddSymbolHook "t2_bor_detect" """if machine['sysbus'].ReadDoubleWord(0x60000078) == 0:
machine['sysbus'].WriteDoubleWord(0x60000078, int(round(machine.ElapsedVirtualTime.TimeElapsed.TotalSeconds * 1000000)))
"""
cpu AddSymbolHook "cancestry_hardware_set_safe_state" """if machine['sysbus'].ReadDoubleWord(0x6000007C) == 0:
machine['sysbus'].WriteDoubleWord(0x6000007C, int(round(machine.ElapsedVirtualTime.TimeElapsed.TotalSeconds * 1000000)))
"""
python "_clog.Logger.Info('[cancestry-hw-bor] step6: brownout symbol hooks installed')"

# Injector preflight readback (console-logged evidence that the peripheral
# loaded and its command interface answers): magic 0x424F5231 ("BOR1"), NRST
# released (1), no injection yet (0), no error (0), SRAM marker intact (0).
# The orchestrator asserts the same values over the monitor and fails closed
# on any mismatch.
python "bus = monitor.Machine['sysbus']; _clog.Logger.Info('[cancestry-hw-bor] step8: injector window magic=0x%08x (expected 0x424F5231) nrst_level=%d (expected 1) inject_count=%d (expected 0) error=%d (expected 0) sram_lost=%d (expected 0)' % (bus.ReadDoubleWord(0x40001000), bus.ReadDoubleWord(0x40001008), bus.ReadDoubleWord(0x4000100C), bus.ReadDoubleWord(0x4000101C), bus.ReadDoubleWord(0x40001018)))"
python "_clog.Logger.Info('[cancestry-hw-bor] step9: include complete, machine left paused')"

# The machine is left PAUSED: the orchestrator alone advances emulation with
# fixed-size `emulation RunFor` quanta. This configuration must NOT be started
# with `start`.
